          <h2>Breakdowns don't check the clock</h2>
          <p>A late finish, a night shift, an early start for the airport, or a drive back from visiting family — vehicles fail at all hours, not just between nine and five. A fault that would be a minor inconvenience at lunchtime can feel a lot more stressful at two in the morning, when the roads are quiet, it's dark, and there's nobody else around to help. That's exactly the situation this service is built for.</p>

          <h2>Why unsociable hours feel harder</h2>
          <p>Several things combine to make a night-time or early-morning breakdown more difficult than a daytime one. Visibility is reduced, both for you assessing the vehicle and for other drivers seeing you at the roadside. There are fewer passers-by and less passing traffic, which can make a stop feel more isolated. Temperatures drop overnight, which is uncomfortable if you're waiting outside and can also be a contributing factor in certain battery and mechanical faults in the first place. None of that changes what we can do for you — it just means the wait can feel longer than it is.</p>

          <h2>We operate around the clock</h2>
          <p>Whatever time your vehicle stops — the middle of the night, first thing on a Sunday, or during a public holiday — call us the same way you would during the day. A recovery vehicle is arranged based on your location and the details you give us, exactly as it would be at any other hour.</p>

          <ul class="checklist">
            <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg> Overnight breakdowns, including the small hours.</li>
            <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg> Weekend breakdowns, Saturday and Sunday alike.</li>
            <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg> Public holidays, including Christmas, New Year and bank holidays.</li>
            <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg> Early-morning breakdowns before the rest of the day has started.</li>
          </ul>

          <div class="callout">
            <p><strong>Staying safe while you wait, after dark.</strong> Keep your hazard lights on and, if you have one, a warning triangle set out where it's safe to place it. Stay well away from moving traffic — behind a barrier if there is one — and keep your phone charged if possible so we can reach you. If you're at all worried about your safety, stay somewhere you feel secure and let us know when you call.</p>
          </div>

          <h2>What if you just need a quick fix, not a tow?</h2>
          <p>Some night-time problems, like a flat battery or being locked out, might not need a full recovery at all. Our <a href="roadside-assistance-aberdeen.html">roadside assistance</a> service covers on-the-spot fixes around the clock too — call and describe the problem, and we'll advise on the best option.</p>
